# Breaks Online: Strudel's breakbeat recipe, the breaks read from the web.
# The track reads clean-breaks' sample map (github.com/yaxu/clean-breaks,
# its strudel.json), and the pad lines give its pads the breaks they name,
# which are all the view fetches. Needs a network, no make samples.
#
#   samples('github:yaxu/clean-breaks')
#   s("amen/4").fit()
#   .slice(8, "<0 1 2 3 4*2 5 6 [6 7]>*2")
#   .cut(1).rarely(ply("2"))
#
# amen/4 is a note four bars long, .slow(4); .cut(1) is the pads' choke group.
tempo 120
track brk sampler PadSampler
samples brk github:yaxu/clean-breaks
pad brk 1 = amen : choke 1
pad brk 2 = funkydrummer : choke 1

clip amen = brk .slow(4) .fit() .slice(8, "<0 1 2 3 4*2 5 6 [6 7]>*2") .rarely(ply(2))
  "c2"

# The Funky Drummer the same way, chopped in sixteen; d2 plays pad 2.
clip funky = brk .slow(2) .fit() .chop(16) .sometimesBy(0.25, mul(speed(-1)))
  "d2"

scene sliced 8: amen
scene chopped 4: funky
arrange sliced chopped
